<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<full-backup-content>
    <!--
      Back up the user's projects and settings. Nothing else.

      This is an allowlist, not a denylist. As soon as one <include> is present,
      Android backs up *only* the included paths, so everything below is omitted
      by default:

        usr/  — the toolchain, rebuilt from the APK on first run. Backing it up
                would restore symlinks pointing at a nativeLibraryDir path that
                no longer exists on the new install, which is worse than absent.
        var/  — conversation database and caches. Large, and restoring a WAL
                mid-checkpoint is a corruption risk.
        apkcli_secrets.xml
              — API keys, encrypted with a hardware-backed Keystore key that
                does not leave the device. The ciphertext would be
                undecryptable after a restore, so backing it up only produces a
                confusing failure.

      Stated as an allowlist on purpose: this is the posture where forgetting to
      add something fails closed. Matching <exclude> entries used to be listed
      here as documentation, but they are redundant under an allowlist and lint
      rejects them (FullBackupContent: "not in an included path").
    -->
    <include domain="file" path="home/" />
    <include domain="sharedpref" path="apkcli_settings.xml" />
</full-backup-content>
